    verification buildScriptHasOneHomeBelowItsUsersStandupGate : Test { :>> id = "6174130d-4cbe-4091-b5e4-22b6aafd2c22"; :>> title = "Sprint 757 standup gate"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-20"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "Layout chosen: a workspace-level build/ directory rather than members/keel-fs/build.rs. A build.rs on keel-fs would run git on every keel-fs build and cascade a rebuild through every dependent when HEAD moves; a script owned by no crate runs only for the crates that name it. Two consequences checked before the move: build/ is not gitignored (git check-ignore build/provenance.rs exits 1), and keel-suite's touched set: wsgraph::candidates (wsgraph.rs:148-161) makes every member a candidate for a changed CODE path no member owns, and SetKeys::read (touched.rs:328) folds unowned code into every member's key - but contentkey::is_code (contentkey.rs:110) listed no build/ arm, so the moved script would have been neither code nor owned: invisible to the set. Found from the first green ladder's receipt (ran = the eight lib rows the six changed manifests reach, stems=[] changed=[]) and read back in source; fixed in this sprint with one predicate arm and its test line before the ladder ran again. The upward definition: a script's owner is neither the crate itself nor in its transitive PATH-dependency closure ([dependencies] plus [build-dependencies]); registry deps are outside the closure by construction."; }
