    verification buildScriptHasOneHomeBelowItsUsersReviewGate : Test { :>> id = "8ba5006f-8a33-4dd1-a610-d2420cb29d61"; :>> title = "Sprint 757 review gate — three passes per D0172"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-20"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "Three passes per D0172. Code read back: crates() reads the root manifest's [workspace].members only, as module_home does, so a nested workspace is unseen (the same failure mode the instrument record names); build = true and an absent key resolve to the crate's own build.rs, which is never upward; the owner lookup is longest-prefix over member directories, so a script under a member's subdirectory is owned by that member. Before the move, --build-edges on the unmoved tree listed five UPWARD rows (guards, hooks, process, serve, write -> keel-cli) and --check went red naming each with its manifest line - the DoD's two had become five, which the sensor now counts rather than a retro. Doc-sync: snModGraph.measures and fbModGraph.title extend to build-script edges; the KNOWN FAILURE MODES and PUBLISHED TO comments name the owner rule, the path-only closure and the ci-probe step; dcBuildScriptDoesNotWatchTheGitIndex's DoD (issue541) now cites build/provenance.rs:53-58 and provenance.rs:37 for the git status call, and dcBuildStampsAFixedWidthCommit's DoD (issue643) cites provenance.rs:32 - both undone items I own. Historical text in Decisions, sprint records and intake keeps keel-cli/build.rs as it was when written."; }
