    verification buildScriptHasOneHomeBelowItsUsersRetroGate : Test { :>> id = "8fb704f8-48ac-4238-8775-88e6620e126c"; :>> title = "Sprint 757 retro gate (autonomous, D0049)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-20"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::analyze; :>> procedureText = "Four findings, avoidable issues scanned (issue585, issue541, issue643). Finding one: the DoD said two members reached up; five did by the time the item was worked, because sprints 736 and 750 copied the build = line from the members before them and nothing counted the reach. The control is this sprint's: modgraph --check is red on the next one, in CI through the probe marker. No new item. Finding two: keel-cli/build.rs was code owned by keel-cli, so a change to it keyed and seeded keel-cli's rows only, never the members baking the stamp; the move would have made it worse - build/ was not a contentkey::is_code path, so the script would have seeded nothing and keyed nothing. The standup text asserted the opposite from touched.rs:328 alone, without reading is_code; the first green ladder's receipt (eight lib rows from the manifests, stems=[] changed=[]) contradicted it and the source confirmed the gap. Fixed in the sprint (contentkey.rs:116 and its test). The class - a claim about a computed set made from one function without its predicate - is D0151's: state the check, or label the suspicion; no automated control fits a sentence in a gate's prose, so no item. Finding three: two undone DoDs cited the old path at fixed lines and were stale before this sprint started (issue541's cited build.rs:47-51 for a block that sits at 53-58 in a file of the same length - the lines were wrong when written, not moved). A line citation in a DoD is a fact about a file at a commit, and the model records no check on it; dcFactsAboutARangeReadTheRange (next on the frontier) is the same class for facts.py, so the finding attaches there rather than opening a second item. Finding four: the # ci-probe header on a Sensor script puts the D0479 layering in CI before dcWorkspaceLayeringIsGuarded lands it as a guard - the two overlap, and the item's DoD should say whether the guard replaces the probe rung or joins it; noted on the retro, resolved when that item is refined."; }
